# ArtesaNFC web (Astro) — Cloudflare Pages static routing.
# Same contract as frontend/_redirects (F-08, Issue #72); only the shell
# location differs: Astro ignores `_`-prefixed page directories, so the
# neutral shells live under /shell/ instead of /_shell/. They are still
# outside /piezas/ and /artesanos/, so no slug can collide with them.
#
# Private certificate route: one shell for any /c/{token}; the token is read
# from location.pathname client-side and never leaves the page except in the
# POST body to the API.
/c/*  /c/  200

# Public detail routes: one neutral shell per entity type; the public API is
# the sole authority on publication. `:slug` (never `*`) so the lists
# /piezas/ and /artesanos/ are not rewritten (docs/QA_PRIVATE_ROUTE.md §5).
/piezas/:slug  /shell/pieza/  200
/piezas/:slug/  /shell/pieza/  200
/artesanos/:slug  /shell/artesano/  200
/artesanos/:slug/  /shell/artesano/  200
